==English==

===Alternative spellings===
* [[ass-backward]], [[ass backward]], [[ass backwards]]

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Oriented [[backwards]], particularly after a [[mishap]].
#: ''The car spun out of control and I ended up '''ass-backwards''' in a ditch.''
# Hopelessly [[misguided]]; having taken the utterly wrong choice.
#: ''No wonder it doesn't work.  The whole design is '''ass-backwards'''.''

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# Moving backwards, that is, [[rear end]] first.
# In a hopelessly misguided manner.
#: ''They did the whole design '''ass-backwards'''.  No wonder it doesn't work.''

====Synonyms====
* [[back-assward]], [[back-asswards]], [[backassward]], [[backasswards]]
* [[bass-ackward]], [[bass-ackwards]], [[bassackward]], [[bassackwards]]

====Quotations====
*'''1966''', Larry Niven, in "At the Core," collected in ''Neutron Star'' (ISBN 0345247949), p. 57,
*:I got the picture then. '''Ass backward''' into the unknown. With the control room at the ship's bottom, it made sense. To a puppeteer, it made sense.

